.TH SPI 3
.SH NAME
spi \- SPI bus, as files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B bind -a #Q /dev

.B /dev/spi0
.B /dev/spi1
.B /dev/spictl
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Spi
is a polled master on the Raspberry Pi 5's header: MOSI GPIO 10, MISO 9,
SCLK 11, chip selects 8 and 7.
The pins become SPI's at the first open.
.PP
A write to
.B spi0
or
.B spi1
is one transfer of at most 8192 bytes with that chip select held low.
SPI sends and receives at once: a read returns what came back during the
last transfer.
.PP
.B Spictl
takes
.BI clock " hz" ,
.BI mode " n"
(0 to 3) and
.BI loop " n" ,
1 joining the block's output to its input inside the chip.
Reading it returns those settings.
.SH SOURCE
.B /os/bcm2712/devspi.c
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR gpio (3),
.IR i2c (3),
.IR pwm (3)
